      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Sertraline 1000 mg once daily is five times the maximum recommended daily dose of 200 mg, and doses this high can cause serious harm, including serotonin syndrome, QT prolongation, and seizures. It may also be a typo, such as 100 mg.\n\nAlso, medication orders need to come from a licensed prescriber who has evaluated the patient. Because you're not a clinician, the order would need to be placed or confirmed by the patient's treating physician or another authorized prescriber.\n\nTo proceed, the prescriber should confirm the intended dose and indication. If they confirm a dose within the labeled range (typically 50\u2013200 mg daily), I can enter that order. If you have the patient's identifiers or the prescriber's name, include them in the request so the order can be attributed correctly. I'd also suggest contacting the medicine service team now to verify this order."
      }
